Falsifies `paging::x86_64::verification::a_block_keeps_address_and_permissions_apart`.

The defect: `Ia32e::block_entry` masks the address with `ADDR_MASK`, the page leaf's
field, instead of down to the block's own alignment. It reads as reuse of a constant
that is already right for pages, and on the pages path it is. In a large-page entry
bit 12 is `PAT` and bits 20:13 (or 29:13) are reserved, so an unaligned `pa` reaching
the encoder sets a reserved bit (a page fault on first touch) or selects a different
memory type, and the `Mapper`'s own alignment refusal is the only thing standing
between that and the hardware.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(block & 0x000f_ffff_ffff_f000 & !address_bits, 0, ...)`
for any `pa` with a bit set between 12 and the block's alignment.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/x86_64.rs b/crates/paging/src/x86_64.rs
index 592f9abe..f391c15e 100644
--- a/crates/paging/src/x86_64.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/x86_64.rs
@@ -190,7 +190,7 @@ impl PageFormat for Ia32e {
         match size {
             PageSize::Size4KiB => Some(Self::leaf_entry(pa, flags)),
             PageSize::Size2MiB | PageSize::Size1GiB => {
-                Some((pa & ADDR_MASK & !(size.bytes() - 1)) | P | PS | Self::attrs(flags))
+                Some((pa & ADDR_MASK) | P | PS | Self::attrs(flags))
             }
         }
     }
